# Serialization Usage Discovery Rule

Detect the presence of serialization functionality to conditionally trigger comprehensive deserialization analysis.

## When Serialization is Detected

If any serialization usage is found, trigger full analysis via 25-deserialization-detection.mdc

## Methods to Detect by Language

### Java
ObjectInputStream.readObject, ObjectOutputStream.writeObject, XMLDecoder.readObject,
Kryo.readClassAndObject, xstream.fromXML, JSON.parseObject, mapper.readValue, yaml.load

### Python
pickle.loads, pickle.load, pickle.dumps, yaml.load, yaml.safe_load,
jsonpickle.decode, dill.loads, marshal.loads

### JavaScript/Node.js
nodeSerialize.unserialize, serialize.unserialize, v8.serialize, v8.deserialize, eval, Function

### C#/.NET
BinaryFormatter.Deserialize, SoapFormatter.Deserialize,
JsonConvert.DeserializeObject, XmlSerializer.Deserialize

### PHP
unserialize, serialize, igbinary_unserialize

### Ruby
Marshal.load, Marshal.dump, YAML.load

### Go
gob.Decode, gob.Encode, json.Unmarshal, xml.Unmarshal

### Rust
bincode::deserialize, serde_json::from_str

## Conditional Rule Triggering

IF serialization_usage_detected THEN
  APPLY 25-deserialization-detection.mdc

## Core Principle

Efficiently identify serialization usage patterns across languages to ensure comprehensive vulnerability analysis is applied when needed.
